# {{lb|en|botany}} On the side that is [[towards]] the [[axis]] or central line, usually on the [[upper]] side.
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=4|text={{...}}it has been transformed, except in a few taxa where lobules are always explanate, into a galeate water-sac, which is formed wholly from the lobule, with the external surface from the '''adaxial''' leaf surface.}}
# {{lb|en|developmental biology}} adjacent to the axis, or in vertebrates the notochord.
#: {{ux|en|In zebrafish, the '''adaxial''' cells are precursors to the embryonic slow muscle fibers.}}

